t}\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t\\,j,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))].$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]=∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $∇f(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2x{y}^{2}))\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2x{y}^{2}))\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{2(1{y}^{2}+x2y\\cdot 0)}{1+4{x}^{2}{y}^{4}}\\,i+\\frac{2(0{y}^{2}+x2y\\cdot 1)}{1+4{x}^{2}{y}^{4}}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{2{y}^{2}}{1+4{x}^{2}{y}^{4}}\\,i+\\frac{4xy}{1+4{x}^{2}{y}^{4}}\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x={e}^{4t}$ and $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t$ into the above to find $∇f(r(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(r(t)) & =\\frac{2(\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t)^{2}}{1+4({e}^{4t})^{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t)^{4}}\\,i+\\frac{4({e}^{4t})(\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t)}{1+4({e}^{4t})^{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t)^{4}}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sin^{2}⁡3t}{1+4{e}^{8t}\\sin^{4}⁡3t}\\,i+\\frac{4{e}^{4t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t}{1+4{e}^{8t}\\sin^{4}⁡3t}\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $r(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{4t})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t)\\,j \\\\  & =4{e}^{4t}\\,i+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))] & =∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(\\frac{2\\sin^{2}⁡3t}{1+4{e}^{8t}\\sin^{4}⁡3t}\\,i+\\frac{4{e}^{4t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t}{1+4{e}^{8t}\\sin^{4}⁡3t}\\,j)\\cdot (4{e}^{4t}\\,i+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t\\,j) \\\\  & =\\frac{8{e}^{4t}\\sin^{2}⁡3t}{1+4{e}^{8t}\\sin^{4}⁡3t}+\\frac{12{e}^{4t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t}{1+4{e}^{8t}\\sin^{4}⁡3t} \\\\  & =\\frac{2{e}^{4t}(4\\sin^{2}⁡3t+6\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t)}{1+4{e}^{8t}\\sin^{4}⁡3t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 1759218653