} + x y^{2}$ and $r(t)=\\ln{\\left(t \\right)}\\,i+3 e^{t}\\,j,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))].$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]=∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $∇f(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x^{2} + x y^{2})\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x^{2} + x y^{2})\\,j \\\\  & =(2 x + y^{2})\\,i+2 x y\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x=\\ln{\\left(t \\right)}$ and $y=3 e^{t}$ into the above to find $∇f(r(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(r(t)) & =(2(\\ln{\\left(t \\right)})+(3 e^{t})^{2})\\,i+2(\\ln{\\left(t \\right)})(3 e^{t})\\,j \\\\  & =(9 e^{2 t} + 2 \\ln{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i+6 e^{t} \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $r(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\ln{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3 e^{t})\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{t}\\,i+3 e^{t}\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))] & =∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =((9 e^{2 t} + 2 \\ln{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i+6 e^{t} \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}\\,j)\\cdot (\\frac{1}{t}\\,i+3 e^{t}\\,j) \\\\  & =((9 e^{2 t} + 2 \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}))\\left(\\frac{1}{t}\\right)+(6 e^{t} \\ln{\\left(t \\right)})(3 e^{t}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2 \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}}{t}+\\frac{9 e^{2 t}}{t}+18 e^{2 t} \\ln{\\left(t \\right)} \\\\  & =18 e^{2 t} \\ln{\\left(t \\right)} + \\frac{9 e^{2 t}}{t} + \\frac{2 \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}}{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536143 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05b2d657-12ba-5244-855a-127cd7306b1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 \\left(6 e^{2 t} + 6 e^{t} \\ln{\\left(t \\right)} + \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536100} {:answer/id #uuid "40d0cfbc-c3e0-5010-8a27-3ad659f00932" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2 \\left(6 e^{2 t} + \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)}{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536117} {:answer/id #uuid "a4cbccd4-10a9-5603-9d7c-31e8c4299e45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{2 \\left(12 t e^{2 t} \\ln{\\left(t \\right)} - 6 e^{2 t} - \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)}{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536152} {:answer/id #uuid "c0a2428f-4efd-534e-b8a5-9d7f8763b84e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2 \\left(12 t e^{2 t} \\ln{\\left(t \\right)} + 6 e^{2 t} + \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)}{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536158} {:answer/id #uuid "dcff26e5-35a3-5a9b-8d7d-385dad335180" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4 \\left(6 t e^{2 t} + t \\ln{\\left(t \\right)} + 3 \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}\\right) e^{t}}{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536167}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c0a2428f-4efd-534e-b8a5-9d7f8763b84e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2 \\left(12 t e^{2 t} \\ln{\\left(t \\right)} + 6 e^{2 t} + \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)}{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536158} :answer-field/id #uuid "07def19c-4051-567c-8664-2166dc149246" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536101}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "82600b93-632f-5ad5-9122-0f9e18ec5a13" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=x^{2} + 3 x y^{2}$ and $r(t)=\\ln{\\left(t \\right)}\\,i+2 e^{t}\\,j,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))].$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]=∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $∇f(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x^{2} + 3 x y^{2})\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x^{2} + 3 x y^{2})\\,j \\\\  & =(2 x + 3 y^{2})\\,i+6 x y\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x=\\ln{\\left(t \\right)}$ and $y=2 e^{t}$ into the above to find $∇f(r(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(r(t)) & =(2(\\ln{\\left(t \\right)})+3(2 e^{t})^{2})\\,i+6(\\ln{\\left(t \\right)})(2 e^{t})\\,j \\\\  & =(12 e^{2 t} + 2 \\ln{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i+12 e^{t} \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $r(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\ln{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2 e^{t})\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{t}\\,i+2 e^{t}\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))] & =∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =((12 e^{2 t} + 2 \\ln{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i+12 e^{t} \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}\\,j)\\cdot (\\frac{1}{t}\\,i+2 e^{t}\\,j) \\\\  & =((12 e^{2 t} + 2 \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}))\\left(\\frac{1}{t}\\right)+(12 e^{t} \\ln{\\left(t \\right)})(2 e^{t}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2 \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}}{t}+\\frac{12 e^{2 t}}{t}+24 e^{2 t} \\ln{\\left(t \\right)} \\\\  & =24 e^{2 t} \\ln{\\left(t \\right)} + \\frac{12 e^{2 t}}{t} + \\frac{2 \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}}{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536144 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c65a274-bf1c-510e-93f7-af87e6992999" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2 t e^{2 t} \\ln{\\left(t \\right)} + e^{2 t} + 2 \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}}{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536109} {:answer/id #uuid "2e078f7c-7fb4-5408-83b3-9282edfe1151" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\left(t e^{2 t} + 2 t \\ln{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 \\ln{\\left(t \\