(r(t))]=∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $∇f(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2x{y}^{2}))\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2x{y}^{2}))\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{2(1{y}^{2}+x2y\\cdot 0)}{1+4{x}^{2}{y}^{4}}\\,i+\\frac{2(0{y}^{2}+x2y\\cdot 1)}{1+4{x}^{2}{y}^{4}}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{2{y}^{2}}{1+4{x}^{2}{y}^{4}}\\,i+\\frac{4xy}{1+4{x}^{2}{y}^{4}}\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x={e}^{3t}$ and $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t$ into the above to find $∇f(r(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(r(t)) & =\\frac{2(\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)^{2}}{1+4({e}^{3t})^{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)^{4}}\\,i+\\frac{4({e}^{3t})(\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)}{1+4({e}^{3t})^{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)^{4}}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sin^{2}⁡2t}{1+4{e}^{6t}\\sin^{4}⁡2t}\\,i+\\frac{4{e}^{3t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t}{1+4{e}^{6t}\\sin^{4}⁡2t}\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $r(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{3t})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)\\,j \\\\  & =3{e}^{3t}\\,i+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))] & =∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(\\frac{2\\sin^{2}⁡2t}{1+4{e}^{6t}\\sin^{4}⁡2t}\\,i+\\frac{4{e}^{3t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t}{1+4{e}^{6t}\\sin^{4}⁡2t}\\,j)\\cdot (3{e}^{3t}\\,i+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,j) \\\\  & =\\frac{6{e}^{3t}\\sin^{2}⁡2t}{1+4{e}^{6t}\\sin^{4}⁡2t}+\\frac{8{e}^{3t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t}{1+4{e}^{6t}\\sin^{4}⁡2t} \\\\  & =\\frac{2{e}^{3t}(3\\sin^{2}⁡2t+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)}{1+4{e}^{6t}\\sin^{4}⁡2t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536169 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51bb9ef3-9793-536d-83c9-dd2d55598726" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/va