solution "The chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]=∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $∇f(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x^{2} + 2 x y^{2})\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x^{2} + 2 x y^{2})\\,j \\\\  & =(2 x + 2 y^{2})\\,i+4 x y\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x=\\ln{\\left(t \\right)}$ and $y=e^{2 t}$ into the above to find $∇f(r(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(r(t)) & =(2(\\ln{\\left(t \\right)})+2(e^{2 t})^{2})\\,i+4(\\ln{\\left(t \\right)})(e^{2 t})\\,j \\\\  & =(2 e^{4 t} + 2 \\ln{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i+4 e^{2 t} \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $r(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\ln{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(e^{2 t})\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{t}\\,i+2 e^{2 t}\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))] & =∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =((2 e^{4 t} + 2 \\ln{\\left(t \\right)})\\,i+4 e^{2 t} \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}\\,j)\\cdot (\\frac{1}{t}\\,i+2 e^{2 t}\\,j) \\\\  & =((2 e^{4 t} + 2 \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}))\\left(\\frac{1}{t}\\right)+(4 e^{2 t} \\ln{\\left(t \\right)})(2 e^{2 t}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2 \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}}{t}+\\frac{2 e^{4 t}}{t}+8 e^{4 t} \\ln{\\left(t \\right)} \\\\  & =8 e^{4 t} \\ln{\\left(t \\right)} + \\frac{2 e^{4 t}}{t} + \\frac{2 \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}}{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542514 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "629864ea-dc15-5e3b-9b4d-74b9fb756902" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-114" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542529} {:answer/id #uuid "8fc460a8-2b92-564e-84d2-f6bf88156beb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-81" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542536} {:answer/id #uuid "cbbf1f2f-d0d2-572a-ab55-c1c9222d13d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542547} {:answer/id #uuid "dad22b74-b2c5-5810-9eb2-eca3707c010c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-117" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542548} {:answer/id #uuid "e076ef3c-3f88-5355-bd0b-9db9eadc6d9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-72" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542550}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8fc460a8-2b92-564e-84d2-f6bf88156beb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-81" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542536} :answer-field/id #uuid "e46b8795-1350-500a-80d1-15be94df06e3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542551}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "034848a3-a1f9-5d8f-b396-bccbb706e96e" :question/problem "Compute the rate of change of the function $f(x,y,z)=3 x z^{2} - 3 y^{3}$ with respect to $t$ along the curve $r(t)=⟨- 3 t,3,\\sqrt{t^{2} - 3}⟩$ at the point $t=2.$" :question/worked-solution "The rate of change of $f(x,y,z)$ with respect to $t$ along the curve $r(t)$ is given by $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))].$ To calculate this, we can use the chain rule.\n\nThe chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]=∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $∇f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3 x z^{2} - 3 y^{3}),\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3 x z^{2} - 3 y^{3}),\\frac{∂}{∂z}(3 x z^{2} - 3 y^{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3 z^{2},- 9 y^{2},6 x z⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x=- 3 t$, $y=3$, $z=\\sqrt{t^{2} - 3}$ into the above to find $∇f(r(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(r(t)) & =⟨3 \\left(\\sqrt{t^{2} - 3}\\right)^{2},- 9 \\cdot 3^{2},6 \\left(- 3 t\\right) \\sqrt{t^{2} - 3}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3 t^{2} - 9,-81,- 18 t \\sqrt{t^{2} - 3}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $r(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(- 3 t),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{t^{2} - 3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3,0,\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{t^{2} - 3}}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))] & =∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =⟨3 t^{2} - 9,-81,- 18 t \\sqrt{t^{2} - 3}⟩\\cdot ⟨-3,0,\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{t^{2} - 3}}⟩ \\\\  & =\\left(3 t^{2} - 9\\right)\\cdot \\left(-3\\right)+\\left(-81\\right)\\cdot \\left(0\\right)+\\left(- 18 t \\sqrt{t^{2} - 3}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{t^{2} - 3}}\\right) \\\\  & =- 9 t^{2} + 27+0- 18 t^{2} \\\\  & =- 27 t^{2} + 27.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of change of $f$ along the curve $r(t)$ at $t=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(2))] & =- 27 (2)^{2} + 27 \\\\  & =-9+0-72 \\\\  & =-81.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542527 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "35332580-e736-51f3-8d53-d1689267dc18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542521} {:answer/id #uuid "64ffb12f-f951-5c6b-b7c6-f1807ed116e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542531} {:answer/id #uuid "745617d4-dbef-5347-9b3e-2ab7c6bdb0de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542533} {:answer/id #uuid "fc9688b1-f72b-59ba-9294-79661d37c55d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542554} {:answer/id #uuid "ffc659a3-2842-5233-9d8a-956412977c32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "26" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542555}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "745617d4-dbef-5347-9b3e-2ab7c6bdb0de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542533} :answer-field/id #uuid "2856210c-b0bb-5727-a27f-b36c68c9cded" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542519}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "53b4c038-e54a-5606-9304-0b269648dd21" :question/problem "Compute the rate of change of the function $f(x,y)=x^{2} - 2 y^{2}$ with respect to $t$ along the curve $r(t)=⟨t,- 3 t + 1⟩$ at the point $t=1.$" :question/worked-solution "The rate of change of $f(x,y)$ with respect to $t$ along the curve $r(t)$ is given by $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))].$ To calculate this, we can use the chain rule.\n\nThe chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]=∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $∇f(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x^{2} - 2 y^{2}),\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x^{2} - 2 y^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2 x,- 4 y⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x=t$, $y=- 3 t + 1$ into the above to find $∇f(r(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(r(t)) & =⟨2 t,- 4 \\left(- 3 t + 1\\right)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2 t,12 t - 4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $r(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(- 3 t + 1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,-3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))] & =∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =⟨2 t,12 t - 4⟩\\cdot ⟨1,-3⟩ \\\\  & =\\left(2 t\\right)\\cdot \\left(1\\right)+\\left(12 t - 4\\right)\\cdot \\left(-3\\right) \\\\  & =- 34 t + 12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of change of $f$ along the curve $r(t)$ at $t=1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(1))] & =- 34 (1) + 12 \\\\  & =-22.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542538 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1da546db-3c69-539d-8533-ef14ece2b34c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542517} {:answer/id #uuid "2fc09648-34f1-5455-b38a-edf896692a5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542520} {:answer/id #uuid "4bb3978c-e581-51df-8b00-a1c1601ddca9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542525} {:answer/id #uuid "975a5f2c-7188-5d8c-9367-ea71bf9eb231" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542537} {:answer/id #uuid "c61528ae-e201-5472-8074-86f9a0167d35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542544}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4bb3978c-e581-51df-8b00-a1c1601ddca9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542525} :answer-field/id #uuid "c26508b5-c575-52f3-b001-a3bcc480b401" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542543}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "9dcc91d6-8511-52d2-b88b-562fac2dd7c9" :question/problem "Compute the rate of change of the function $f(x,y)=- 3 x^{2} + 3 y^{2}$ with respect to $t$ along the curve $r(t)=⟨- t + 2,2 t⟩$ at the point $t=-1.$" :question/worked-solution "The rate of change of $f(x,y)$ with respect to $t$ along the curve $r(t)$ is given by $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))].$ To calculate this, we can use the chain rule.\n\nThe chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]=∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $∇f(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂x}(- 3 x^{2} + 3 y^{2}),\\frac{∂}{∂y}(- 3 x^{2} + 3 y^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨- 6 x,6 y⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x=- t + 2$, $y=2 t$ into the above to find $∇f(r(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(r(t)) & =⟨- 6 \\left(- t + 2\\right),6 \\cdot 2 t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6 t - 12,12 t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $r(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(- t + 2),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2 t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))] & =∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =⟨6 t - 12,12 t⟩\\cdot ⟨-1,2⟩ \\\\  & =\\left(6 t - 12\\right)\\cdot \\left(-1\\right)+\\left(12 t\\right)\\cdot \\left(2\\right) \\\\  & =18 t + 12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of change of $f$ along the curve $r(t)$ at $t=-1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(-1))] & =18 (-1) + 12 \\\\  & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542540 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1553423d-6619-5296-aa27-6dfa538e24eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "78" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542516} {:answer/id #uuid "1e419297-22b4-5144-949a-5be3e729d78c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-204" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542518} {:answer/id #uuid "5bcd6ddb-a207-5fad-a229-e213b01e5b8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542528} {:answer/id #uuid "f100370d-dab2-5f2f-94c0-ca4059d2a5e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-144" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542552} {:answer/id #uuid "fa06d295-a30b-5d75-a328-9f9ffade51bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-84" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542553}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fa06d295-a30b-5d75-a328-9f9ffade51bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-84" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542553} :answer-field/id #uuid "c8ed3c28-7663-5d3f-a250-39410e6adb51" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542545}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "a445e341-e46b-5bbe-83fe-c9e1dc16e770" :question/problem "Compute the rate of change of the function $f(x,y)=3 x^{2} - 3 y^{2}$ with respect to $t$ along the curve $r(t)=⟨- 3 t + 2,2 t - 1⟩$ at the point $t=-2.$" :question/worked-solution "The rate of change of $f(x,y)$ with respect to $t$ along the curve $r(t)$ is given by $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))].$ To calculate this, we can use the chain rule.\n\nThe chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]=∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $∇f(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3 x^{2} - 3 y^{2}),\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3 x^{2} - 3 y^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6 x,- 6 y⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x=- 3 t + 2$, $y=2 t - 1$ into the above to find $∇f(r(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(r(t)) & =⟨6 \\left(- 3 t + 2\\right),- 6 \\left(2 t - 1\\right)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨- 18 t + 12,- 12 t + 6⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $r(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(- 3 t + 2),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2 t - 1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))] & =∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =⟨- 18 t + 12,- 12 t + 6⟩\\cdot ⟨-3,2⟩ \\\\  & =\\left(- 18 t + 12\\right)\\cdot \\left(-3\\right)+\\left(- 12 t + 6\\right)\\cdot \\left(2\\right) \\\\  & =30 t - 24.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of change of $f$ along the curve $r(t)$ at $t=-2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(-2))] & =30 (-2) - 24 \\\\  & =-84.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542541 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10a2909f-aed0-5af2-b387-7f8903415e75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542515} {:answer/id #uuid "64f6d064-4d09-5ab2-acff-66f1b85596b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542530} {:answer/id #uuid "a190bb06-3da8-5c89-b3a7-dafbff724ab9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542539} {:answer/id #uuid "a74ba907-6998-5a4f-b6f4-82147ccc7fff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-44" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542542} {:answer/id #uuid "c9250b77-adfa-55a2-9bc2-f29bce32c28f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542546}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a190bb06-3da8-5c89-b3a7-dafbff724ab9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542539} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a7b6273-78bd-5548-919c-67a2237339f3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542534}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "a6d7ded6-d4bb-5d2b-990f-e6ceb3a10aad" :question/problem "Compute the rate of change of the function $f(x,y)=x^{2} - y^{2}$ with respect to $t$ along the curve $r(t)=⟨- 3 t + 1,- t - 1⟩$ at the point $t=-2.$" :question/worked-solution "The rate of change of $f(x,y)$ with respect to $t$ along the curve $r(t)$ is given by $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))].$ To calculate this, we can use the chain rule.\n\nThe chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]=∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $∇f(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x^{2} - y^{2}),\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x^{2} - y^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2 x,- 2 y⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x=- 3 t + 1$, $y=- t - 1$ into the above to find $∇f(r(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(r(t)) & =⟨2 \\left(- 3 t + 1\\right),- 2 \\left(- t - 1\\right)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨- 6 t + 2,2 t + 2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $r(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(- 3 t + 1),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(- t - 1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))] & =∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =⟨- 6 t + 2,2 t + 2⟩\\cdot ⟨-3,-1⟩ \\\\  & =\\left(- 6 t + 2\\right)\\cdot \\left(-3\\right)+\\left(2 t + 2\\right)\\cdot \\left(-1\\right) \\\\  & =16 t - 8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of change of $f$ along the curve $r(t)$ at $t=-2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(-2))] & =16 (-2) - 8 \\\\  & =-40.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542549 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "370db119-3661-5ef2-b2af-6ee498d06182" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542522} {:answer/id #uuid "4ae7aec4-1d83-5eea-8940-6f5cbdb71e5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542524} {:answer/id #uuid "51c65ed2-f0a3-5583-90c1-01d3b3865b32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542526} {:answer/id #uuid "6b912948-1642-5e4e-a34a-7231c206e0a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542532} {:answer/id #uuid "7c87e7bb-1e6b-5577-9c25-5750c2d40b40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542535}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4ae7aec4-1d83-5eea-8940-6f5cbdb71e5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542524} :answer-field/id #uuid "3a9d6bbb-fcd7-51d9-a68b-5d578c88f08e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542523}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "de3e4415-7d66-5c90-8a1e-b6b9a369cc6a" :question/problem "Compute the rate of change of the function $f(x,y)=- 3 x^{2} - 2 y^{2}$ with respect to $t$ along the curve $r(t)=⟨t - 2,3 t + 2⟩$ at the point $t=0.$" :question/worked-solution "The rate of change of $f(x,y)$ with respect to $t$ along the curve $r(t)$ is given by $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))].$ To calculate this, we can use the chain rule.\n\nThe chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]=∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $∇f(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂x}(- 3 x^{2} - 2 y^{2}),\\frac{∂}{∂y}(- 3 x^{2} - 2 y^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨- 6 x,- 4 y⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x=t - 2$, $y=3 t + 2$ into the above to find $∇f(r(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(r(t)) & =⟨- 6 \\left(t - 2\\right),- 4 \\left(3 t + 2\\right)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨- 6 t + 12,- 12 t - 8⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $r(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t - 2),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3 t + 2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))] & =∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =⟨- 6 t + 12,- 12 t - 8⟩\\cdot ⟨1,3⟩ \\\\  & =\\left(- 6 t + 12\\right)\\cdot \\left(1\\right)+\\left(- 12 t - 8\\right)\\cdot \\left(3\\right) \\\\  & =- 42 t - 12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of change of $f$ along the curve $r(t)$ at $t=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(0))] & =- 42 (0) - 12 \\\\  & =-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552629 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3300b6f4-a3cb-5719-834a-3ce95f706574" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2 \\left(7 \\pi + 24\\right) e^{\\frac{2 \\pi}{3}}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552630} {:answer/id #uuid "a173706e-6c6d-5503-aa64-3fbd8adb1d59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8 \\pi e^{\\frac{4 \\pi}{3}}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552659} {:answer/id #uuid "aeb3ce33-88d3-5cf7-ac21-58ac8f8ca664" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9 + 12 \\pi + 4 \\pi^{2} + 4 \\pi^{2} e^{\\frac{4 \\pi}{3}}}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552663} {:answer/id #uuid "dac1d9b0-5582-5825-bd06-d6346490288e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\left(3 + 4 \\pi\\right) e^{\\frac{2 \\pi}{3}}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552671} {:answer/id #uuid "e63ee131-898b-5cf9-a3cf-85e2960cb2c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4 \\left(3 + 2 \\pi\\right) e^{\\frac{2 \\pi}{3}}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552674}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e63ee131-898b-5cf9-a3cf-85e2960cb2c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4 \\left(3 + 2 \\pi\\right) e^{\\frac{2 \\pi}{3}}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552674} :answer-field/id #uuid "ebe94a29-5154-5b7b-a526-237832ee07d6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552675}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "32141bb4-29d3-5922-9dd9-4806a03ebce3" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]$ at $t=\\frac{\\pi}{6}$ given that $∇f(x,y)=\\left(y \\left(\\ln{\\left(x \\right)} + 1\\right)\\right)\\,i+\\left(x \\ln{\\left(x \\right)}\\right)\\,j$ and $r(t)=\\left(e^{4 t}\\right)\\,i+\\left(\\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\right)\\,j.$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]=∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nIn addition, we've been given that\n\n$$\n∇f(x,y)=\\left(y \\left(\\ln{\\left(x \\right)} + 1\\right)\\right)\\,i+\\left(x \\ln{\\left(x \\right)}\\right)\\,j.\n$$\n\nFirst, we substitute $x=e^{4 t}$ and $y=\\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}$ into $∇f(x,y)$ to find $∇f(r(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(r(t)) & =\\left(y \\left(\\ln{\\left(x \\right)} + 1\\right)\\right)\\,i+\\left(x \\ln{\\left(x \\right)}\\right)\\,j\\Big|_{x=e^{4 t},\\,y=\\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}} \\\\  & =\\left(\\left(4 t + 1\\right) \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\right)\\,i+\\left(4 t e^{4 t}\\right)\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $r(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}\\left(e^{4 t}\\right)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}\\left(\\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\right)\\,j \\\\  & =\\left(4 e^{4 t}\\right)\\,i+\\left(3 \\cos{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\right)\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))] & =∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =\\left(\\left(\\left(4 t + 1\\right) \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\right)\\,i+\\left(4 t e^{4 t}\\right)\\,j\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\left(4 e^{4 t}\\right)\\,i+\\left(3 \\cos{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\right)\\,j\\right) \\\\  & =\\left(\\left(4 t + 1\\right) \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\right)\\cdot \\left(4 e^{4 t}\\right)+\\left(4 t e^{4 t}\\right)\\cdot \\left(3 \\cos{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\right) \\\\  & =\\left(16 t e^{4 t} \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)} + 4 e^{4 t} \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\right)+\\left(12 t e^{4 t} \\cos{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\right) \\\\  & =4 \\left(4 t \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)} + 3 t \\cos{\\left(3 t \\right)} + \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\right) e^{4 t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating the above at $t=\\frac{\\pi}{6},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]\\Big|_{t=\\frac{\\pi}{6}} & =4 \\left(4 t \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)} + 3 t \\cos{\\left(3 t \\right)} + \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\right) e^{4 t}\\Big|_{t=\\frac{\\pi}{6}} \\\\  & =\\left(\\frac{4 \\left(3 + 2 \\pi\\right) e^{\\frac{2 \\pi}{3}}}{3}\\right)+\\left(0\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{4 \\left(3 + 2 \\pi\\right) e^{\\frac{2 \\pi}{3}}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552637 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "745d9116-ef9b-541d-bed2-643d16922eb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552643} {:answer/id #uuid "7f7ba0a8-a6bd-54d4-aa58-70bb7223e88a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552647} {:answer/id #uuid "d7b593eb-f9bf-53ce-bf40-d2147e6f6ffe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552668} {:answer/id #uuid "f7270bd1-41dc-56f7-a7ef-3f45cc8da6d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/m