fc51" :question/problem "If $f(x,y,z)=4\\left(yz\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\right)$ and $r(t)={(t + 1)}^{2}\\,i+{e}^{(t + 1)}\\,j+{e}^{(t + 1)}\\,k,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))].$" :question/worked-solution "The chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]=∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $∇f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(4\\left(yz\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\right))\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(4\\left(yz\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\right))\\,j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(4\\left(yz\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\right))\\,k \\\\  & =(4\\left(-yz\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\right))\\,i+(4\\left(+z\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\right))\\,j+(4\\left(+y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\right))\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x={(t + 1)}^{2},y={e}^{(t + 1)},$ and $z={e}^{(t + 1)}$ into the above to find $∇f(r(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(r(t)) & =(4\\left(-{e}^{2(t + 1)}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({(t + 1)}^{2})\\right))\\,i+(4\\left(+{e}^{(t + 1)}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({(t + 1)}^{2})\\right))\\,j+(4\\left(+{e}^{(t + 1)}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({(t + 1)}^{2})\\right))\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $r(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({(t + 1)}^{2})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{(t + 1)})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{(t + 1)})\\,k \\\\  & =(2(t + 1))\\,i+(+{e}^{(t + 1)})\\,j+(+{e}^{(t + 1)})\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))] & =∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =((4\\left(-{e}^{2(t + 1)}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({(t + 1)}^{2})\\right))\\,i+(4\\left(+{e}^{(t + 1)}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({(t + 1)}^{2})\\right))\\,j+(4\\left(+{e}^{(t + 1)}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({(t + 1)}^{2})\\right))\\,k)\\cdot ((2(t + 1))\\,i+(+{e}^{(t + 1)})\\,j+(+{e}^{(t + 1)})\\,k) \\\\  & =4\\left(-2(t + 1){e}^{2(t + 1)}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({(t + 1)}^{2})+{e}^{(t + 1)}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({(t + 1)}^{2})\\cdot {e}^{(t + 1)}+{e}^{(t + 1)}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({(t + 1)}^{2})\\cdot {e}^{(t + 1)}\\right) \\\\  & =4\\left(-2(t + 1){e}^{2(t + 1)}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({(t + 1)}^{2})+2{e}^{2(t + 1)}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({(t + 1)}^{2})\\right) \\\\  & =4\\left(2{e}^{2(t + 1)}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡({(t + 1)}^{2})-(t + 1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡({(t + 1)}^{2}))\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186555998 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06d1d6bd-d89b-5bad-bd17-b50341f803cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 2 {e}^{2(t - 2)} \\sin((t - 2)^{2}) (t - 2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555960} {:answer/id #uuid "4664a78f-effb-5ddf-988f-356dddd95a7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 \\cos((t - 2)^{2}) {e}^{2(t - 2)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555971} {:answer/id #uuid "8f66985e-58fb-59d3-98c8-1287b1ccd811" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{2(t - 2)}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡({(t - 2)}^{2})-(t - 2)\\operatorname{sin}⁡({(t - 2)}^{2}))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555991} {:answer/id #uuid "b5f54656-e29a-5b5b-890b-fac4665b8674" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{(t - 2)} \\left(2 \\cos((t - 2)^{2}) - {e}^{(t - 2)} \\sin((t - 2)^{2})\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555997} {:answer/id #uuid "ee89e640-8825-5ae1-b367-7b5359189bc2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2(t - 2)} \\left(2 \\cos((t - 2)^{2}) - \\sin((t - 2)^{2})\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186556005}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8f66985e-58fb-59d3-98c8-1287b1ccd811" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{2(t - 2)}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡({(t - 2)}^{2})-(t - 2)\\operatorname{sin}⁡({(t - 2)}^{2}))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592